Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: the software adapter passes Chromium 155's fallback gate

Chromium 155 returns no adapter from CreatePreferredAdapter's fallback pass
unless WebGPU runs unsafe, because the fallback adapter is SwiftShader. The
profile's software adapter on a Linux host with no GPU is found only by that
pass, so from 155 a persona that claims a WebGPU adapter served none there:
"No available adapters." on 0.5.0 where 0.4.4 served the claimed adapter,
measured in the same Debian 13 container.

The pass runs again when CanUseProfileSoftwareWebGPU admitted the profile
path. That instance loads only SwiftShader from the one trusted directory
(0056), and RequestAdapterImpl already refuses a page's own
forceFallbackAdapter on it, so pages still cannot ask for SwiftShader.

diff --git a/gpu/command_buffer/service/webgpu_decoder_impl.cc b/gpu/command_buffer/service/webgpu_decoder_impl.cc
index 45c1e18e18..5f248ba1b2 100644
--- a/gpu/command_buffer/service/webgpu_decoder_impl.cc
+++ b/gpu/command_buffer/service/webgpu_decoder_impl.cc
@@ -2082,9 +2082,12 @@ wgpu::Adapter WebGPUDecoderImpl::CreatePreferredAdapter(
     wgpu::FeatureLevel feature_level,
     bool webgpu_on_vk_gl_interop) const {
   // The fallback adapter is SwiftShader, which is only allowed with
-  // --enable-unsafe-webgpu. Don't make Dawn load it otherwise.
+  // --enable-unsafe-webgpu. Don't make Dawn load it otherwise. The profile's
+  // software adapter is the exception: it is SwiftShader from the one trusted
+  // directory, admitted by CanUseProfileSoftwareWebGPU, and a page asking for
+  // the fallback adapter is refused before this point.
   const bool allow_fallback_adapter =
-      safety_level_ == webgpu::SafetyLevel::kUnsafe;
+      safety_level_ == webgpu::SafetyLevel::kUnsafe || profile_software_webgpu_;
   if (force_fallback && !allow_fallback_adapter) {
     return nullptr;
   }
